ation\n\n### 3. **`internal/domain/` - Entity Definitions**\n**Complete entity definitions exist:**\n\n**Issue Claim Entity (`domain/issue.go`)**:\n```go\ntype IssueClaim struct {\n    ID           int64       `json:\"id\"`\n    RepoFullName string      `json:\"repo_full_name\"` // GitHub repo full name\n    IssueNumber  int         `json:\"issue_number\"`   // GitHub issue number\n    IssueTitle   string      `json:\"issue_title\"`    // Cached issue title\n    Status       IssueStatus `json:\"status\"`         // Status from IssueStatus enum\n    SessionID    string      `json:\"session_id\"`     // Owner's session ID\n    ClaimedAt    *time.Time  `json:\"claimed_at\"`     // Claim timestamp\n    UpdatedAt    time.Time   `json:\"updated_at\"`     // Last update time\n}\n\ntype IssueStatus string\n\nconst (\n    IssueIdle       IssueStatus = \"idle\"        // Available\n    IssueClaimed    IssueStatus = \"claimed\"     // Claimed by a session\n    IssueFixing     IssueStatus = \"fixing\"      // Being developed\n    IssueReadyForPR IssueStatus = \"ready-for-pr\" // Ready for PR\n    IssuePRCreated  IssueStatus = \"pr-created\"  // PR created\n    IssueTesting    IssueStatus = \"testing\"     // Testing in progress\n    IssueReviewing  IssueStatus = \"reviewing\"   // Under review\n    IssueMerged     IssueStatus = \"merged\"      // Completed\n    IssueRejected   IssueStatus = \"rejected\"    // Rejected\n)\n```\n\n**Other Domain Entities**:\n- `Session` - Tracks Claude Code session metadata\n- `Project` - Projects worked on\n- `Machine` - Machine information\n\n### 4. **Store Interface and Implementation for Issue Claims**\n**Status: Empty files**\n- `store/issue_store.go` - Empty (should contain IssueClaim store interface)\n- `store/store.go` - Empty (should contain main store interface)\n- `store/sqlite.go` - Empty (should contain SQLite implementation)\n\n### 5. **HTTP Router/Handler Setup**\n**Status: Empty files**\n- `api/router.go` - Empty (should contain router setup)\n- `api/issue_handler.go` - Empty (should contain issue claim handlers)\n- `api/session_handler.go` - Empty (should contain session handlers)\n- `api/health_handler.go` - Empty\n\n### 6. **API Handler Patterns**\n**No existing patterns to follow** - all handler files are empty.\n\n## Key Findings\n\n1. **The project is a skeleton** - Domain models are defined but all backend implementation is missing\n2. **Main functionality is in proxy mode** - The main.go shows it's primarily a reverse proxy for Claude Code\n3. **Backend server is planned but not implemented** - The structure exists but code is empty\n4. **Issue claim domain model is complete** - Ready for backend implementation\n5. **Empty test files suggest planned API endpoints** for issue and session management\n\nThe project appears to be in early development stages where the core proxy functionality is implemented, but the backend server components (for issue claims, session management, etc.) are planned but not yet implemented.\n\nWould you like me to help implement any specific parts of the backend based on the domain models that are already defined?","background_tasks":[],"session_crons":[]}
